{"text": "3,0. 3.\nCHARCOAL CIGARETTE - JAPAN January 15, 1980\n\nintroduction\n\nThe charcoal filter segment of the Japan cigarette market\nhas had a phenomenal growth. In 1969 charcoal filter\naccounted for 16.8% of import and only 1.6\u00a2 of domestic\nSales. By 1979 they accounted for 71.2% of US imports\nand 48.5% of domestic sales. The necessity of a charcoal\nfilter cigarette to compete in Japan is not a matter\nfor discussion, it is a fact supported by widespread\nacceptance of the charcoal filter concept by Japanese\nsmokers. The entire non-charcoal segment has been heavily\neroded by the strength of charcoal filter sales. Lark,\n@ non-brand in the US*, accounts for that 71.2% share of\nUs imports, with a 1978 volume in excess of 2 billion\nunits, Kent was second, and declining with the rest of\nthe non-charcoal market, with 8.38 share and 1978 volume\nof 243 million. For further information please refer to\nappendix 1.\n\nWhat to do?\n\nTo gain a meaningful share of the Japan Market we must\ndevelop a charcoal filter cigarette with other qualities\nwhich are acceptable to the Japanese smoker. Beczuse of\night restrictions on marketing and advertising, @ situ~\n\u2018ation which will only slightly improve through continuous\nfndustry pressure, the charcoal brand developed must be\nassociated with a brand already well-known in Japan.\n\nThe brand should also have a tar content not less than\nlgng. nor nore than ldng. (as measured by the Japanese) -\nThe Japan monopoly has been reducing the tar and nicotine\ncontent of its major brands, and launched two new \u201clow\ntar\" brands in 1977, \"Just\" and \"Mild Seven\". \u201cJust\u201d at\ntng. of nicotine has not achieved a meaningful share\ngoing from 0.6\u00a2 to 0.88 from 1977 thru 1978. \"Mild Seven\u201d\n2 lang. is A rising star. It averaged 6.4\u00a2 share in 1977\nand by the end of 1978 it had achieved 27.68 share (please\nSee appendix 2). While therg are other, factors which\nContributed to acceptance of Mild Seven\u2019, the lack of growth\nof \"Just\" in comparison in probably reflective of a taste\nFejection of too mild a cigarette at Sng. .\n\n+ yotal Lark sales in US in 1978 were approximately 4-0\nbi:\nLion units. 621063833", "words": [{"text": "3,0.", "x0": 231, "y0": 234, "x1": 267, "y1": 243, "conf": 53.0}, {"text": "3.", "x0": 277, "y0": 234, "x1": 290, "y1": 242, "conf": 50.0}, {"text": "CHARCOAL", "x0": 231, "y0": 253, "x1": 293, "y1": 262, "conf": 88.0}, {"text": "CIGARETTE", "x0": 301, "y0": 251, "x1": 370, "y1": 260, "conf": 87.0}, {"text": "-", "x0": 378, "y0": 254, "x1": 385, "y1": 256, "conf": 65.0}, {"text": "JAPAN", "x0": 394, "y0": 250, "x1": 431, "y1": 259, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "January", "x0": 517, "y0": 248, "x1": 570, "y1": 258, "conf": 90.0}, {"text": "15,", "x0": 579, "y0": 246, "x1": 598, "y1": 257, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "1980", "x0": 610, "y0": 246, "x1": 638, "y1": 255, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": "introduction", "x0": 234, "y0": 283, "x1": 325, "y1": 294, "conf": 47.0}, {"text": "The", "x0": 233, "y0": 310, "x1": 255, "y1": 319, "conf": 88.0}, {"text": "charcoal", "x0": 264, "y0": 308, "x1": 324, "y1": 319, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": "filter", "x0": 334, "y0": 308, "x1": 379, "y1": 318, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "segment", "x0": 388, "y0": 307, "x1": 441, "y1": 318, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "of", "x0": 449, "y0": 306, "x1": 464, "y1": 315, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "the", "x0": 472, "y0": 306, "x1": 495, "y1": 315, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Japan", "x0": 503, "y0": 306, "x1": 541, "y1": 314, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": "cigarette", "x0": 550, "y0": 304, "x1": 618, "y1": 315, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "market", "x0": 626, "y0": 303, "x1": 671, "y1": 311, "conf": 89.0}, {"text": "has", "x0": 234, "y0": 323, "x1": 255, "y1": 332, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "had", "x0": 265, "y0": 322, "x1": 287, "y1": 332, "conf": 75.0}, {"text": "a", "x0": 296, "y0": 324, "x1": 302, "y1": 331, "conf": 75.0}, {"text": "phenomenal", "x0": 311, "y0": 321, "x1": 387, "